# 2026-11-21 17:14:36.183244
+Create model.py now: compact code, no docstrings, minimal comments (reply capped near 2,000 tokens — be economical). It implements the forecasting math for our GTA VI trophy entry:
+- imports: math; from datetime import datetime, timezone
+- RELEASE = datetime(2026, 11, 19, tzinfo=timezone.utc)
+- Z = [-1.644854, -0.674490, 0.0, 0.674490, 1.644854]; PRIOR = {'platinum': 0.55, 'gold': 0.75, 'silver': 0.90, 'bronze': 1.00}
+- clamp(v, lo, hi); logit(rate): clamp rate to [0.01, 99.99] first, p = rate/100, return log(p/(1-p)); inv_logit(l): return 100/(1+exp(-l))
+- hours(ts): parse ISO-8601 (may end with Z, may carry fractional seconds) with datetime.fromisoformat after replacing a trailing 'Z' with '+00:00'; return hours since RELEASE as float
+- wls(u, y, w): weighted least squares; return (slope, weighted RMS residual); guard zero denominators (slope 0.0, rms 0.0)
+- forecast(points, tier, x_t, horizon_days): points is a non-empty list of (x, rate) sorted by x. r_last = last rate; x_last = last x. If len(points) < 3 or all rates equal: b = PRIOR[tier]; s_fit = 0.30. Else: u = [log(1+x) for x in xs]; y = [logit(r) for r in rates]; w = [1 + x/x_last if x_last > 0 else 1.0 for x in xs]; slope, rms = wls(u, y, w); s_fit = max(rms, 0.30); b = 0.65*slope + 0.35*PRIOR[tier]. g = b * (log(1 + x_t) - log(1 + x_last)); damp = 1 / (1 + exp((r_last - 50) / 12)); med = logit(r_last) + g * (0.35 + 0.65 * damp). rate = inv_logit(med); if r_last < 20: rate = min(rate, min(99.5, max(r_last * 8, r_last + 12))); rate = clamp(rate, max(0.01, r_last * 0.25), 99.99); med = logit(rate). s = sqrt((0.5 * sqrt(horizon_days))**2 + (0.6 * s_fit)**2 + 0.22**2). qs = [round(clamp(inv_logit(med + z * s), 0.01, 99.99), 4) for z in Z]; enforce non-decreasing (each item = max(item, previous)); return qs.
+Only model.py in this reply.

